      "title": "Say hello your way",
      "goal": "Greet, introduce yourself and say goodbye freely for 30 seconds.",
      "culture": {
        "title": "La bise or a handshake?",
        "body": "In France friends and family greet each other with la bise — light cheek-to-cheek kisses. The number of kisses depends on the region: two is most common, but you may get three or even four in some areas. In Belgium one kiss is common, and in French-speaking Switzerland three is typical. In business, or when meeting someone for the first time, a handshake is the safe choice. In Québec people switch to tu more readily, and a bise or a hug is mostly for close friends and family. Belgians say À tantôt ! (see you later today), and in Québec you'll often hear Bonne fin de semaine ! (have a nice weekend).",
        "regions": [
          "FR",
          "BE",
          "CH",
          "CA"
        ]
      },
      "phrases": [
        {
          "t": "Bonne soirée !",
          "n": "Have a nice evening!"
        },
        {
          "t": "Bon week-end !",
